+    /// Initial congestion window in bytes for every connection (CUBIC).
+    /// `None` keeps quinn's default (about ten packets).
+    ///
+    /// quinn paces one congestion window over 0.8 RTT and does not grow the
+    /// window while the sender is application limited, so a connection that
+    /// mostly idles sends a burst of S bytes in about 0.8 * S / window round
+    /// trips. A window several times the largest expected burst lets that
+    /// burst leave in one flight. Loss still shrinks the window as usual.
+    pub initial_congestion_window: Option<u64>,
 }
 
